{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>To you</b> — because my ancestors were prophets, unlike the ancestors of other nations, that you gave him wisdom and might above all the wise." "And he said: <b>You have made known to me</b> — for to him alone the secret was made known." "And he said: <b>before you</b> — he and his companions, as if to say: not by my merit alone did you make known to me this secret." "And he said: <b>You have made known to me</b> — for he made it known to them:"], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The subject of 'you gave him' shifts to a third person singular; translated literally as the Hebrew stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:15.433375695Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}